I suggest we don't jump directly into writing lots of code. We'll build it in a clean order so you understand what you're doing.

🚀 Portfolio Development Roadmap
1. Project setup
First we'll make sure your project is properly configured:

my-portfolio/
├── src/
│   ├── assets/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── sections/
│   ├── App.jsx
│   ├── main.jsx
│   └── index.css
├── public/
├── package.json
└── vite.config.js

We'll configure:

React + Vite
Tailwind CSS
Fonts
Colors
Global styles
Responsive design
2. Decide the portfolio structure
A good developer portfolio could have:

Navbar
   ↓
Hero
   ↓
About Me
   ↓
Skills
   ↓
Projects
   ↓
Experience / Education
   ↓
Services
   ↓
Contact
   ↓
Footer

You don't necessarily need all of these. We can choose based on your actual experience and goals.

3. Build reusable React components
Instead of putting everything into App.jsx, we'll create components such as:

components/
├── Navbar.jsx
├── Button.jsx
├── ProjectCard.jsx
├── SkillCard.jsx
└── Footer.jsx

sections/
├── Hero.jsx
├── About.jsx
├── Skills.jsx
├── Projects.jsx
└── Contact.jsx

This will make your portfolio much easier to maintain.

4. Design the Hero section
This is the first thing visitors see.

For example:

Hi, I'm [Your Name]
Frontend Developer
I build modern, responsive web experiences.

Then:

[ View My Work ]   [ Contact Me ]

We can add your photo, illustration, animation, or other visual elements depending on the style you want.

5. Build the Projects section
This is one of the most important sections for a developer portfolio.

Each project can show:

Project screenshot
Project name
Short description
Technologies used
Live demo
GitHub repository
For example:

┌─────────────────────────────┐
│                             │
│       Project Image         │
│                             │
├─────────────────────────────┤
│ E-commerce Website          │
│                             │
│ React • Tailwind • API      │
│                             │
│ [Live Demo] [GitHub]        │
└─────────────────────────────┘

6. Make it responsive
We'll test the portfolio on:

📱 Mobile
   ↓
📱 Tablet
   ↓
💻 Laptop
   ↓
🖥️ Large Desktop

Don't design only for your laptop. A good portfolio should look intentional at every size.

7. Add polish
Once everything works, we can add things like:

Smooth scrolling
Hover effects
Subtle animations
Dark/light mode
Page transitions
Project filtering
Mobile navigation
Loading effects
The key is not to overdo animations. Your projects and content should remain the focus.

8. Deploy it
Finally we'll deploy it so you have a real URL you can put on your:

CV/resume
LinkedIn
GitHub
Job applications